{
  "summary": "Adds a checkbox in GUI send and fee-bumping confirmation dialogs allowing users to export unsigned transactions as PSBTv2 instead of the default PSBTv0. In the core codebase, it also removes the default version argument from the `PartiallySignedTransaction(const CMutableTransaction&)` constructor, requiring callers to explicitly choose the version.",
  "problem": "Many hardware wallets and external signing tools do not support BIP-370 (PSBTv2). Because Bitcoin Core previously defaulted to PSBTv2, GUI users exporting PSBTs to sign on external hardware encountered incompatibility errors, even though the GUI does not yet make use of PSBTv2-specific features.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit message: 'PSBTv0 is set by default since the GUI can't do anything interesting with PSBTv2 yet.'",
    "Author description cites fixing issue #36518."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
